    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Blue Kuri squash is&nbsp;a Japanese Kabocha-type winter squash with a flattened, globe shape and a distinct blue-grey skin. It has dense, sweet, and creamy yellow-orange flesh with a rich, nutty flavor and a thin, edible skin. This variety stores very well and is versatile in the kitchen, used for roasting, soups, pies, and other sweet or savory dishes.&nbsp;</span></p>",
